      "case": "filesystem/glob/parse-grammar-battery",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "Four acceptances a port gets wrong by being sensible, and one rejection it gets wrong by being lenient. [!a-z] is ACCEPTED and its negate flag is stored (glob.go:104-107, :127) though nothing downstream reads it, so the element row records char_range true 97 122; [\\ufffd-a] is ACCEPTED because readRangeRune only errors on decode size 0 or 1 (glob.go:142-147), so a properly encoded U+FFFD is a legal bound and a port testing rune == U+FFFD rejects it, while [\\xff-\\xff] IS rejected as invalid UTF-8; [z-a] is accepted unvalidated; and }, , and a,b are ordinary literals at top level while {} is a group of ONE empty member and {,} a group of two. The element lists are the second half: a//b is four elements (literal, slash, slash, literal), never a normalized one, and ** is a single star_star, never two stars -- the two representations that every later case depends on and that a rendering alone cannot tell apart.",
      "operation": "tsc/internal/glob/glob.go:Parse",
      "order_sensitive": true,
      "subject": "glob.Glob",
      "hosts": [
        "any"
      ],
      "host_note": "any"
