      "case": "filesystem/glob/parse-nested-residual",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "The nested flag is a behavioural switch, not decoration, and this carries the lost-argument control: a port that dropped the argument, or that hardcoded it the way Parse does at glob.go:48, produces the nested=false column twice. Every pattern here answers differently under the two flags except \"a\" and \"\": a,b} yields glob \"a\" residual \",b}\" nested and glob \"a,b}\" residual \"\" non-nested; } yields an EMPTY element list and residual \"}\" nested, consuming nothing, against a one-literal glob non-nested. The residual is the other half: it is what the '{' arm loops on (glob.go:78-89) and Parse throws away (glob.go:48), so a port that returned only the glob would be unable to parse a group at all.",
      "operation": "tsc/internal/glob/glob.go:parse",
      "order_sensitive": true,
      "subject": "glob.parse",
