      "case": "filesystem/glob/element-render-direct",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "The seven element renderings, reached one at a time instead of through a pattern, so each one's contribution is separable. The discriminating rows are the ones a pattern cannot produce: charRange{true,'a','z'} renders \"[a-z]\" exactly like charRange{false,'a','z'}, which is the negate flag being dropped rather than a parser choice; charRange{false,'z','a'} and charRange{true,U+10FFFF,U+0000} render inverted bounds unvalidated; a nil group, an empty group and a group whose one member is the empty Glob all render \"{}\", because strings.Join over no parts is \"\" (glob.go:207); and literal(\"\\xff\") renders one byte, which a port storing a literal as String cannot do. Two star elements and one starStar element BOTH render \"**\": the rendering cannot tell the representations apart, which is exactly why the parse rows in filesystem/glob/parse-grammar-battery are the ones that resolve it -- ** parses to a single star_star.",
      "operation": "tsc/internal/glob/glob.go:charRange.String",
      "order_sensitive": true,
      "subject": "glob.element",
      "hosts": [
        "any"
      ],
      "host_note": "any"
