      "case": "filesystem/glob/match-star-separator",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "Three pin behaviours that a correct-looking port contradicts. (1) A '*' immediately followed by '/' makes the pattern unmatchable against any input carrying that separator: */a vs x/a, src/*/x vs src/y/x, *x/y vs ax/y, */* vs a/b and **/*/x vs a/b/x are all FALSE, because the star arm consumes the separator through split (glob.go:266) and then hands the slash element an input that has already lost it -- while ?/a, [a-z]/b and {a,b}/c against the same shape are TRUE, so the defect is the star arm alone and not separators in general. (2) A separator RUN in the pattern is unmatchable from either side: a//b matches neither a/b nor a//b, while a/b matches a/b, a//b and a///b, because one slash element consumes a whole run (glob.go:228-230) and two demand two runs. (3) Match PANICS on an input whose separator run reaches the end -- a/ vs a/ and / vs / -- because that same loop has no length guard, and panics again on a nil receiver. A port that returns true, false or an error for any of the five in (1), or that normalizes a run, or that answers instead of failing in (3), diverges.",
