      "case": "filesystem/glob/match-group-branch-buffer",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "Carries this bucket's mutation-leaking control. The group arm reuses ONE branch buffer across alternatives and resets it with branch[:0] before each (glob.go:305-309); a port that forgets the reset, or that appends the trailing elements once outside the loop, answers FALSE for {a,b,c}x vs \"bx\" and \"cx\" where the pin answers true, while still answering true for \"ax\" -- so only the second and third alternatives expose it. {a,ab}c and {ab,a}c vs abc pin that the arm returns on the first member that matches with the REMAINING elements appended, not on the first member that matches a prefix. An empty alternative is live: {a,} matches both \"a\" and \"\", so a port that prunes empty alternatives changes the result. A nil group and an empty group both match nothing, including \"\". The foreign element is the default arm (glob.go:326-327), which no pinned element type can reach.",
