      "case": "filesystem/glob/split-separator-runs",
      "dialect": "lsp",
      "discriminates": "A whole run of consecutive separators collapses into one boundary, and a run that reaches the end yields rest \"\" rather than a string of slashes: split(\"a//\") is (\"a\",\"\") and split(\"//\") is (\"\",\"\"), indistinguishable from split(\"a\") and split(\"\") in the second field. A port that split on a single separator returns (\"a\",\"/\") for \"a//\" and flips both callers -- the star arm would then see a leftover separator in the segment remainder and the starStar backtrack would loop over a different sequence of suffixes. The doc comment above it claims it returns nil rest, which is false: it returns the empty string, and no caller could tell the difference in Go anyway.",
